{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794415240,"nonce":"nUBHKP2RdM3sZSOlA22uwOyLSg8=","message":"Item 2, the rest of what will be built for now: lent callbacks.\n\nA function takes a Haxe function as `impl Fn(..) -\u003e Result\u003cT, E\u003e` (or `FnMut`,\n`FnOnce`), generic in `E`. Arguments are `bool`, `i32`, `f64`, up to four; the\nresult is one of those or `()`. A type parameter is allowed on a function for\nthis and nothing else.\n\nGenerated (`crates/hxn-gen/src/lent.rs`):\n\n- C ABI: an `hxn_callback` by value; the adapter passes the library a closure\n  over `Callback::invoke`, so a failed call is an `Err(Failure)`.\n- HashLink: a closure parameter (`Pid_Nb` and so on), called through a\n  generated trampoline that boxes the arguments. `hxn-hl` gained `box_f64`,\n  `box_bool` and their unboxing.\n- hxcpp: a `Dynamic` parameter in the glue and a trampoline there.\n- One function pointer type and one trampoline a shape of function, per\n  library.\n- Haxe: the method wraps what it was passed (null, or false from a function\n  that returns nothing, says it threw) and runs its whole body inside\n  `hxn.Callback.during`. The HashLink method emitter now builds a list of\n  statements like the hxcpp one, so both share that step.\n\nFixture: `each`, `test`, `scaled_by`, `ask`, `from_fn`, `attempt` and the\nexisting `apply` on `Counter`; checked by `callbacks()` in `Generated.hx`,\nincluding that the exception a lent function throws is the very object the\ncaller catches, that it is thrown even when the library swallows the failure,\nand that re-entering the object from its own callback fails with \"in use\".\nPasses on Ash (three modes), stock HashLink, hxcpp, Ash wasm and Emscripten.\n\nNot built:\n\n- Text, bytes or objects to or from a lent function.\n- A function kept across calls. That stays on the Haxe side by design (see\n  the callbacks issue): the class keeps it in a field and lends it each time.\n  The generator does not write that field or its setter.\n- `async fn`, for the reason given in the previous comment.","files":null}]}